# Wave W17-W (Mt. Apex — North): zenith stone — frost-rimmed stone at the east register: pale ashlar courses carrying frost flecks struck across their cap and face, the east door’s winter drawn into the wall itself (design: frost creeping in from the snowy east door; the climb holds stand byte-preserved in this wall’s field, mechanic data untouched). Mt. Apex — North’s own wall — split from Central’s seam-shadowed spine stone by the frost and the paleness entire, and from South’s jamb stone by register: the top floor’s wall is weather, the hall’s wall is doors.
